WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.272
April 18th and 19th, 2020: Gabriel Wortman killed twenty-two people over thirteen hours.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:14.727
April 28th, 2020: Commissioner Lucki promised the Minister's office and the PMO firearms details for Bill C-21 support.

00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:23.056
May 1st, 2020: the Order in Council banning approximately fifteen hundred firearm models was executed without a parliamentary vote.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:29.999
Superintendent Darren Campbell documented in writing that Commissioner Lucki stated she had promised the Minister and the PMO.

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:35.727
The RCMP failed to issue a province-wide Alert Ready notification despite having functional capacity.

00:00:35.727 --> 00:00:41.988
The Mass Casualty Commission, Volume 5, documented pressure from federal officials for political purposes.

00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:44.022
Twenty-two Canadians were killed.

00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:48.931
One hundred and thirty recommendations were issued on March 30th, 2023.

00:00:48.931 --> 00:00:52.795
The tragedy was used as a political instrument before the victims were buried.
